# CQ-20 · event-participants
#
# Question: For every Event in the corpus: who does what to whom, with what, and
#           for whom?
# Persona:  P3 — director / creative technologist. The shot-list sentence, read
#           back out of the graph the same way the caption renderer reads it.
# Spec:     docs/vson.md §5.6 (`vso:Event`, thematic roles); §2 clause C6
# Form:     SELECT — one row per Event
# Note:     Each role is OPTIONAL because arity is per-verb: `charge` has an
#           agent and a patient and no instrument, `give` binds theme and
#           recipient instead of patient, and an inner join on all five would
#           silently drop every Event that is not `strike`. That per-verb
#           variation is the reason §5.6 keeps the role inventory closed and
#           coarse rather than per-predicate. C6 makes the lemma required, so it
#           is the one column that cannot be absent.
PREFIX vso: <https://w3id.org/vson/v1/ontology#>

SELECT ?doc ?event ?lemma ?agent ?patient ?theme ?recipient ?instrument
WHERE {
  GRAPH ?doc {
    ?event a vso:Event ; vso:lemma ?lemma .
    OPTIONAL { ?event vso:agent      ?agent }
    OPTIONAL { ?event vso:patient    ?patient }
    OPTIONAL { ?event vso:theme      ?theme }
    OPTIONAL { ?event vso:recipient  ?recipient }
    OPTIONAL { ?event vso:instrument ?instrument }
  }
}
ORDER BY ?doc ?event
